            "review_title": "Review at Cinderella Bar",
            "review_text": "DanCarmo\nSan Antonio, Texas27 contributions\n0\nUnderrated Gem - The Filipina Cover Bands Rock!\nNov 2018 • Friends\nI don't know why this bar is always half empty the cover bands that play, the women and men singers alike, really have the pipes to play out the standard rock tunes, mostly American music, the vocals are always on top. \n\nOK so the set-up is a bit weird - you walk in a low round doorway and step down into the bar seating area in front of a stage, it's kinda dark, but the waitresses are friendly and fast to serve your order. It's located in a strange location right off Le Thanh Ton across from a great outdoor BBQ place (highly recommended!) in Little Japan area but can be easily found. I went there several nights while on an extended stay in SGN. \n\nBeers are priced a little higher (same as western prices!) because the music is free. Limited spirts on menu. If you like live music you should at least stop in for a 30-minute set, they will surprise you just how good they are!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten November 18, 2018",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-14",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
